#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "1. Introduction {#1-introduction}"
msgstr "1. Pengenalan {#1-introduction}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Bits, gates, and circuits are the basic building blocks of quantum computing. You will learn quantum computation with the circuit model using quantum bits and gates, and also review the superposition, measurement, and entanglement.\n"
msgstr "Bit, gate, dan litar adalah blok binaan asas pengkomputeran kuantum. Anda akan belajar pengkomputeran kuantum dengan model litar menggunakan bit kuantum dan gate, serta mengulang kaji superposisi, pengukuran, dan keterjeratan.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In this lesson you will learn:\n"
"- Single-qubit gates\n"
"- Bloch sphere\n"
"- Superposition\n"
"- Measurement\n"
"- Two-qubit gates and entanglement state\n"
msgstr ""
"Dalam pelajaran ini Anda akan belajar:\n"
"- get qubit tunggal\n"
"- Sfera Bloch\n"
"- Superposisi\n"
"- Pengukuran\n"
"- get dua qubit dan keadaan jalinan\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "At the end of this lecture, you will learn about circuit depth, which is essential for utility-scale quantum computing.\n"
msgstr "Di akhir kuliah ini, Anda akan belajar tentang kedalaman litar, yang penting untuk pengkomputeran kuantum berskala utiliti.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "2. Computation as a diagram {#2-computation-as-a-diagram}"
msgstr "2. Pengiraan sebagai gambar rajah {#2-computation-as-a-diagram}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "When using qubits or bits, we need to manipulate them in order to turn the inputs we have into the outputs we need. For the simplest programs with very few bits, it is useful to represent this process in a diagram known as a *circuit diagram*.\n"
msgstr "Apabila menggunakan qubit atau bit, kita perlu memanipulasinya supaya input yang ada boleh diubah kepada output yang diperlukan. Untuk atur cara paling mudah dengan sangat sedikit bit, adalah berguna untuk mewakili proses ini dalam gambar rajah yang dikenali sebagai *gambar rajah litar*.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The bottom-left figure is an example of a classical circuit, and the bottom-right figure is an example of a quantum circuit. In both cases, the inputs are on the left and the outputs are on the right, while the operations are represented by symbols. The symbols used for the operations are called “gates”, mostly for historical reasons.\n"
msgstr "Rajah di bawah sebelah kiri adalah contoh litar klasik, dan rajah di bawah sebelah kanan adalah contoh litar kuantum. Dalam kedua-dua kes, input berada di sebelah kiri dan output berada di sebelah kanan, manakala operasi diwakili oleh simbol. Simbol yang digunakan untuk operasi dipanggil \"gate\", kebanyakannya atas sebab sejarah.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![\"classical logic and quantum circuit\"](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-quantum-computing/bits-gates-and-circuits/classical-vs-quantum.avif)\n"
msgstr "![\"litar logik klasik dan litar kuantum\"](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-quantum-computing/bits-gates-and-circuits/classical-vs-quantum.avif)\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "3. Single-qubit quantum gate {#3-single-qubit-quantum-gate}"
msgstr "3. get kuantum qubit tunggal {#3-single-qubit-quantum-gate}"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "3.1 Quantum state and Bloch sphere {#31-quantum-state-and-bloch-sphere}"
msgstr "3.1 Keadaan kuantum dan sfera Bloch {#31-quantum-state-and-bloch-sphere}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A qubit's state is represented as a superposition of $|0\\rangle$ and $|1\\rangle$. An arbitrary quantum state is represented as\n"
msgstr "Keadaan qubit diwakili sebagai superposisi $|0\\rangle$ dan $|1\\rangle$. Keadaan kuantum sembarangan diwakili sebagai\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"|\\psi\\rangle =\\alpha|0\\rangle+ \\beta|1\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"|\\psi\\rangle =\\alpha|0\\rangle+ \\beta|1\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "where $\\alpha$ and $\\beta$ are complex numbers such that $|\\alpha|^2+|\\beta|^2=1$.\n"
msgstr "di mana $\\alpha$ dan $\\beta$ ialah nombor kompleks sedemikian rupa sehingga $|\\alpha|^2+|\\beta|^2=1$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "$|0\\rangle$ and $|1\\rangle$ are vectors in the two-dimensional complex vector space:\n"
msgstr "$|0\\rangle$ dan $|1\\rangle$ ialah vektor dalam ruang vektor kompleks dua dimensi:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"|0\\rangle = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 \\\\0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix},\n"
"|1\\rangle = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0\\\\1\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"|0\\rangle = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 \\\\0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix},\n"
"|1\\rangle = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0\\\\1\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Therefore, an arbitrary quantum state is also represented as\n"
msgstr "Oleh itu, keadaan kuantum sembarangan juga diwakili sebagai\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"|\\psi\\rangle = \\alpha\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 \\\\ 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix} + \\beta\\begin{pmatrix}0\\\\\n"
"1\n"
"\\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha \\\\ \\beta\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"|\\psi\\rangle = \\alpha\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 \\\\ 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix} + \\beta\\begin{pmatrix}0\\\\\n"
"1\n"
"\\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha \\\\ \\beta\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "From this, we can see that the state of a quantum bit is a unit vector in a two-dimensional complex inner product space with an orthonormal basis of $|0\\rangle$ and $|1\\rangle$. It is normalized to 1.\n"
msgstr "Daripada ini, kita dapat lihat bahawa keadaan bit kuantum adalah vektor unit dalam ruang hasil darab dalaman kompleks dua dimensi dengan asas ortonormal $|0\\rangle$ dan $|1\\rangle$. Ia dinormalkan kepada 1.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle\\psi|\\psi\\rangle = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha^* & \\beta^*\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha \\\\\n"
"\\beta\n"
"\\end{pmatrix} = 1\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle\\psi|\\psi\\rangle = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha^* & \\beta^*\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha \\\\\n"
"\\beta\n"
"\\end{pmatrix} = 1\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$ |\\psi\\rangle =\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha \\\\ \\beta\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}$ is also called the statevector.\n"
msgstr ""
"$ |\\psi\\rangle =\\begin\\{pmatrix\\}\n"
"\\alpha \\\\ \\beta\n"
"\\end\\{pmatrix\\}$ juga dikenali sebagai statevector.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A single-qubit quantum state is also represented as\n"
msgstr "Keadaan kuantum qubit tunggal juga boleh diwakili sebagai\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"|\\psi\\rangle\n"
"=\\cos\\frac{\\theta}{2}|0\\rangle+e^{i\\varphi}\\sin\\frac{\\theta}{2}|1\\rangle\n"
"=\\left( \\begin{pmatrix} \\cos\\frac{\\theta}{2}\\\\ e^{i\\varphi}\\sin\\frac{\\theta}{2}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\\right)\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"|\\psi\\rangle\n"
"=\\cos\\frac{\\theta}{2}|0\\rangle+e^{i\\varphi}\\sin\\frac{\\theta}{2}|1\\rangle\n"
"=\\left( \\begin{pmatrix} \\cos\\frac{\\theta}{2}\\\\ e^{i\\varphi}\\sin\\frac{\\theta}{2}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\\right)\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "where $\\theta$ and $\\varphi$ are the angles of the Bloch sphere in the following figure.\n"
msgstr "di mana $\\theta$ dan $\\varphi$ ialah sudut sfera Bloch dalam rajah berikut.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Bloch sphere](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-quantum-computing/bits-gates-and-circuits/bloch.avif)\n"
"In the next few code cells, we will build up basic calculations from constituent pieces in Qiskit. We'll construct an empty circuit and then add quantum operations, discussing the gates and visualizing their effects as we go.\n"
"You can run the cell by \"Shift\" + \"Enter\". Import the libraries first.\n"
msgstr ""
"![Sfera Bloch](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-quantum-computing/bits-gates-and-circuits/bloch.avif)\n"
"Dalam beberapa sel kod berikut, kita akan membina pengiraan asas daripada komponen-komponen dalam Qiskit. Kita akan membina litar kosong kemudian menambah operasi kuantum, membincangkan gate dan menggambarkan kesannya semasa proses.\n"
"Anda boleh menjalankan sel dengan menekan \"Shift\" + \"Enter\". Import perpustakaan dahulu.\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Prepare the quantum circuit {#prepare-the-quantum-circuit}"
msgstr "Sediakan litar kuantum {#prepare-the-quantum-circuit}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We will create and draw a single-qubit circuit.\n"
msgstr "Kita akan mencipta dan melukis litar qubit tunggal.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-quantum-computing/bits-gates-and-circuits/extracted-outputs/fdef9137-9e39-4b05-afa9-9091766053f6-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-quantum-computing/bits-gates-and-circuits/extracted-outputs/fdef9137-9e39-4b05-afa9-9091766053f6-0.avif)\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "X gate {#x-gate}"
msgstr "get X {#x-gate}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The X gate is a $\\pi$ rotation around the $x$ axis of the Bloch sphere.\n"
"Applying the X gate to $|0\\rangle$ results in $|1\\rangle$, and applying the X gate to $|1\\rangle$ results in $|0\\rangle$, so it is an operation similar to the classical NOT gate, and is also known as bit flip. The matrix representation of the X gate is below.\n"
msgstr ""
"get X ialah putaran $\\pi$ mengelilingi paksi $x$ sfera Bloch.\n"
"Menggunakan get X pada $|0\\rangle$ menghasilkan $|1\\rangle$, dan menggunakan get X pada $|1\\rangle$ menghasilkan $|0\\rangle$, jadi ia adalah operasi yang serupa dengan get NOT klasik, dan juga dikenali sebagai bit flip. Perwakilan matriks get X adalah seperti berikut.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"X = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0 & 1 \\\\\n"
"1 & 0 \\\\\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"X = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0 & 1 \\\\\n"
"1 & 0 \\\\\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-quantum-computing/bits-gates-and-circuits/extracted-outputs/b3468430-0cbc-44ab-bd21-901436662a4b-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-quantum-computing/bits-gates-and-circuits/extracted-outputs/b3468430-0cbc-44ab-bd21-901436662a4b-0.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In IBM Quantum&reg;, the initial state is set to $|0\\rangle$, so the quantum circuit above in matrix representation is\n"
msgstr "Dalam IBM Quantum&reg;, keadaan awal ditetapkan kepada $|0\\rangle$, jadi litar kuantum di atas dalam perwakilan matriks adalah\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"X|0\\rangle=  \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0 & 1 \\\\\n"
"1 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 \\\\ 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
" =\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0 \\\\ 1\n"
"\\end{pmatrix} = |1\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"X|0\\rangle=  \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0 & 1 \\\\\n"
"1 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 \\\\ 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
" =\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0 \\\\ 1\n"
"\\end{pmatrix} = |1\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Next, let's run this circuit using a statevector simulator.\n"
msgstr "Seterusnya, mari jalankan litar ini menggunakan simulator statevector.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-quantum-computing/bits-gates-and-circuits/extracted-outputs/efb727e8-f51e-4903-aa0f-e4c099316815-1.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-quantum-computing/bits-gates-and-circuits/extracted-outputs/efb727e8-f51e-4903-aa0f-e4c099316815-1.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Vertical vector is displayed as row vector, with complex numbers (the imaginary part is indexed by $j$ ).\n"
msgstr "Vektor menegak dipaparkan sebagai vektor baris, dengan nombor kompleks (bahagian imaginar diindeks dengan $j$).\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "H gate {#h-gate}"
msgstr "get H {#h-gate}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The Hadamard gate is a $\\pi$ rotation around an axis halfway between the $x$ and $z$ axes on the Bloch sphere. Applying the H gate to $|0\\rangle$ creates a superposition state such as $\\frac{|0\\rangle + |1\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}}$. The matrix representation of the H gate is below.\n"
msgstr "get Hadamard ialah putaran $\\pi$ mengelilingi paksi yang berada di tengah-tengah antara paksi $x$ dan $z$ pada sfera Bloch. Menggunakan get H pada $|0\\rangle$ menghasilkan keadaan superposisi seperti $\\frac{|0\\rangle + |1\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}}$. Perwakilan matriks get H adalah seperti berikut.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"H = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 & 1 \\\\\n"
"1 & -1 \\\\\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"H = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 & 1 \\\\\n"
"1 & -1 \\\\\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-quantum-computing/bits-gates-and-circuits/extracted-outputs/574c35f0-26a9-423a-8d65-7140ba7398e3-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-quantum-computing/bits-gates-and-circuits/extracted-outputs/574c35f0-26a9-423a-8d65-7140ba7398e3-0.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-quantum-computing/bits-gates-and-circuits/extracted-outputs/7adf0e93-6db3-4aa8-800f-c91c8cc46001-1.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-quantum-computing/bits-gates-and-circuits/extracted-outputs/7adf0e93-6db3-4aa8-800f-c91c8cc46001-1.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This is\n"
"$$\n"
"H|0\\rangle= \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 & 1 \\\\\n"
"1 & -1\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 \\\\0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
" =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 \\\\\n"
"1\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"=\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0.707 \\\\\n"
"0.707\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(|0\\rangle+|1\\rangle)\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"Ini adalah\n"
"$$\n"
"H|0\\rangle= \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 & 1 \\\\\n"
"1 & -1\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 \\\\0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
" =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 \\\\\n"
"1\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"=\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0.707 \\\\\n"
"0.707\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(|0\\rangle+|1\\rangle)\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This superposition state is so common and important, that it is given its own symbol:\n"
msgstr "Keadaan superposisi ini sangat biasa dan penting sehingga ia diberi simbolnya sendiri:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"|+\\rangle \\equiv \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(|0\\rangle+|1\\rangle).\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"|+\\rangle \\equiv \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(|0\\rangle+|1\\rangle).\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "By applying the $H$ gate on the $|0\\rangle$, we created a superposition of $|0\\rangle$ and $|1\\rangle$ where measurement in the computational basis (along z in the Bloch sphere picture) would give you each state with equal probabilities.\n"
msgstr "Dengan menggunakan get $H$ pada $|0\\rangle$, kita telah mencipta superposisi $|0\\rangle$ dan $|1\\rangle$ di mana pengukuran dalam asas komputasi (sepanjang z dalam gambaran sfera Bloch) akan memberikan setiap keadaan dengan kebarangkalian yang sama.\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "$|-\\rangle$ state {#rangle-state}"
msgstr "Keadaan $|-\\rangle$ {#rangle-state}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"You might have guessed that there is a corresponding  $|-\\rangle$ state:\n"
"$$\n"
"|-\\rangle \\equiv \\frac{|0\\rangle -|1\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}}.\n"
"$$\n"
"To create this state, first apply an X gate to make $|1\\rangle$, then apply an H gate.\n"
msgstr ""
"Mungkin Anda sudah meneka bahawa terdapat keadaan $|-\\rangle$ yang sepadan:\n"
"$$\n"
"|-\\rangle \\equiv \\frac{|0\\rangle -|1\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}}.\n"
"$$\n"
"Untuk mencipta keadaan ini, mula-mula gunakan get X untuk membuat $|1\\rangle$, kemudian gunakan get H.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-quantum-computing/bits-gates-and-circuits/extracted-outputs/b8e96fc4-6708-415e-b8fc-ac69eaeae750-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-quantum-computing/bits-gates-and-circuits/extracted-outputs/b8e96fc4-6708-415e-b8fc-ac69eaeae750-0.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-quantum-computing/bits-gates-and-circuits/extracted-outputs/f42b82aa-7a15-4f81-8530-b997d4c6e0de-1.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-quantum-computing/bits-gates-and-circuits/extracted-outputs/f42b82aa-7a15-4f81-8530-b997d4c6e0de-1.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This is\n"
msgstr "Ini adalah\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"H|1\\rangle= \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 & 1 \\\\\\\n"
"1 & -1\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0 \\\\\\\n"
"1\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
" =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 \\\\\\\n"
"-1\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"=\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0.707 \\\\\\\n"
"-0.707\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(|0\\rangle-|1\\rangle) = |-\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"H|1\\rangle= \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 & 1 \\\\\\\n"
"1 & -1\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0 \\\\\\\n"
"1\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
" =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 \\\\\\\n"
"-1\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"=\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0.707 \\\\\\\n"
"-0.707\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(|0\\rangle-|1\\rangle) = |-\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Applying the $H$ gate on $|1\\rangle$ results in an equal superposition of $|0\\rangle$ and $|1\\rangle$, but the sign of $|1\\rangle$ is negative.\n"
msgstr "Menggunakan get $H$ pada $|1\\rangle$ menghasilkan superposisi sama rata antara $|0\\rangle$ dan $|1\\rangle$, tetapi tanda $|1\\rangle$ adalah negatif.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "3.2 Single-qubit quantum state and unitary evolution {#32-single-qubit-quantum-state-and-unitary-evolution}"
msgstr "3.2 Keadaan kuantum qubit tunggal dan evolusi unitari {#32-single-qubit-quantum-state-and-unitary-evolution}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The actions of all the gates we have seen so far have been *unitary*, which means they can be represented by a unitary operator. In other words, the output state can be obtained by acting on the initial state with a unitary matrix:\n"
msgstr "Tindakan semua get yang telah kita lihat setakat ini adalah *unitari*, bermakna ia boleh diwakili oleh pengoperasi unitari. Dengan kata lain, keadaan output boleh diperoleh dengan menggunakan matriks unitari pada keadaan awal:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"|\\psi^{'}\\rangle = U|\\psi\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"|\\psi^{'}\\rangle = U|\\psi\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A unitary matrix is a matrix satisfying\n"
msgstr "Matriks unitari ialah matriks yang memenuhi syarat\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"U^{\\dagger}U =U U^{\\dagger} = I.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"U^{\\dagger}U =U U^{\\dagger} = I.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In terms of quantum computer operation, we would say that applying a quantum gate to the qubit evolves the quantum state. Common single-qubit gates include the following.\n"
msgstr "Dari segi operasi komputer kuantum, kita boleh katakan bahawa menggunakan get kuantum pada qubit akan mengevolusikan keadaan kuantum tersebut. get qubit tunggal yang lazim termasuklah yang berikut.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Pauli gates:\n"
msgstr "get Pauli:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"X = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0 & 1 \\\\\n"
"1 & 0 \\\\\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= |0\\rangle \\langle 1|+|1\\rangle \\langle 0|\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"X = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0 & 1 \\\\\n"
"1 & 0 \\\\\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= |0\\rangle \\langle 1|+|1\\rangle \\langle 0|\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"Y = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0 & -i \\\\\n"
"i & 0 \\\\\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= -i|0\\rangle \\langle 1|+i|1\\rangle \\langle 0|\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"Y = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0 & -i \\\\\n"
"i & 0 \\\\\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= -i|0\\rangle \\langle 1|+i|1\\rangle \\langle 0|\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"Z = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 & 0 \\\\\n"
"0 & -1 \\\\\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= |0\\rangle \\langle 0|-|1\\rangle \\langle 1|\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"Z = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 & 0 \\\\\n"
"0 & -1 \\\\\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= |0\\rangle \\langle 0|-|1\\rangle \\langle 1|\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"where the outer product was calculated as follows:\n"
"$$\n"
"|0\\rangle \\langle 0|=\n"
"\\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"1 \\\\\n"
"0\n"
"\\end{bmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"1 & 0\n"
"\\end{bmatrix}\n"
"=\\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"1 & 0 \\\\\n"
"0 & 0 \\\\\n"
"\\end{bmatrix}, \\quad\n"
"|1\\rangle \\langle 0|=\n"
"\\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"0 \\\\\n"
"1\n"
"\\end{bmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"1 & 0\n"
"\\end{bmatrix}\n"
"=\\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"0 & 0 \\\\\n"
"1 & 0 \\\\\n"
"\\end{bmatrix}, \\quad\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"di mana hasil darab luar dikira seperti berikut:\n"
"$$\n"
"|0\\rangle \\langle 0|=\n"
"\\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"1 \\\\\n"
"0\n"
"\\end{bmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"1 & 0\n"
"\\end{bmatrix}\n"
"=\\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"1 & 0 \\\\\n"
"0 & 0 \\\\\n"
"\\end{bmatrix}, \\quad\n"
"|1\\rangle \\langle 0|=\n"
"\\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"0 \\\\\n"
"1\n"
"\\end{bmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"1 & 0\n"
"\\end{bmatrix}\n"
"=\\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"0 & 0 \\\\\n"
"1 & 0 \\\\\n"
"\\end{bmatrix}, \\quad\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"|0\\rangle \\langle 1|=\n"
"\\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"1 \\\\\n"
"0\n"
"\\end{bmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"0 & 1\n"
"\\end{bmatrix}\n"
"=\\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"0 & 1 \\\\\n"
"0 & 0 \\\\\n"
"\\end{bmatrix}, \\quad\n"
"|1\\rangle \\langle 1|=\n"
"\\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"0 \\\\\n"
"1\n"
"\\end{bmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"0 & 1\n"
"\\end{bmatrix}\n"
"=\\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"0 & 0 \\\\\n"
"0 & 1 \\\\\n"
"\\end{bmatrix}, \\quad\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"|0\\rangle \\langle 1|=\n"
"\\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"1 \\\\\n"
"0\n"
"\\end{bmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"0 & 1\n"
"\\end{bmatrix}\n"
"=\\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"0 & 1 \\\\\n"
"0 & 0 \\\\\n"
"\\end{bmatrix}, \\quad\n"
"|1\\rangle \\langle 1|=\n"
"\\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"0 \\\\\n"
"1\n"
"\\end{bmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"0 & 1\n"
"\\end{bmatrix}\n"
"=\\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"0 & 0 \\\\\n"
"0 & 1 \\\\\n"
"\\end{bmatrix}, \\quad\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Other typical single-qubit gates:\n"
"$$\n"
"H= \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"1 & 1 \\\\\n"
"1 & -1 \\\\\n"
"\\end{bmatrix},\\quad\n"
"S = \\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"1 & 0 \\\\\n"
"0 & i \\\\\n"
"\\end{bmatrix}, \\quad\n"
"T = \\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"1 & 0 \\\\\n"
"0 & exp(i\\pi/4) \\\\\n"
"\\end{bmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"get qubit tunggal biasa yang lain:\n"
"$$\n"
"H= \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"1 & 1 \\\\\n"
"1 & -1 \\\\\n"
"\\end{bmatrix},\\quad\n"
"S = \\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"1 & 0 \\\\\n"
"0 & i \\\\\n"
"\\end{bmatrix}, \\quad\n"
"T = \\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"1 & 0 \\\\\n"
"0 & exp(i\\pi/4) \\\\\n"
"\\end{bmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"R_x(\\theta) = e^{-i\\theta X/2} = cos\\frac{\\theta}{2}I - i sin \\frac{\\theta}{2}X = \\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"cos\\frac{\\theta}{2} &  -i sin \\frac{\\theta}{2} \\\\\n"
"-i sin \\frac{\\theta}{2} & cos\\frac{\\theta}{2} \\\\\n"
"\\end{bmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"R_x(\\theta) = e^{-i\\theta X/2} = cos\\frac{\\theta}{2}I - i sin \\frac{\\theta}{2}X = \\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"cos\\frac{\\theta}{2} &  -i sin \\frac{\\theta}{2} \\\\\n"
"-i sin \\frac{\\theta}{2} & cos\\frac{\\theta}{2} \\\\\n"
"\\end{bmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"R_y(\\theta) = e^{-i\\theta Y/2} = cos\\frac{\\theta}{2}I - i sin \\frac{\\theta}{2}Y = \\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"cos\\frac{\\theta}{2} &  - sin \\frac{\\theta}{2} \\\\\n"
"sin \\frac{\\theta}{2} & cos\\frac{\\theta}{2} \\\\\n"
"\\end{bmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"R_y(\\theta) = e^{-i\\theta Y/2} = cos\\frac{\\theta}{2}I - i sin \\frac{\\theta}{2}Y = \\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"cos\\frac{\\theta}{2} &  - sin \\frac{\\theta}{2} \\\\\n"
"sin \\frac{\\theta}{2} & cos\\frac{\\theta}{2} \\\\\n"
"\\end{bmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"R_z(\\theta) = e^{-i\\theta Z/2} = cos\\frac{\\theta}{2}I - i sin \\frac{\\theta}{2}Z = \\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"e^{-i\\theta /2} &  0 \\\\\n"
"0 & e^{i\\theta /2} \\\\\n"
"\\end{bmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"R_z(\\theta) = e^{-i\\theta Z/2} = cos\\frac{\\theta}{2}I - i sin \\frac{\\theta}{2}Z = \\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"e^{-i\\theta /2} &  0 \\\\\n"
"0 & e^{i\\theta /2} \\\\\n"
"\\end{bmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The meaning and use of these are described in more detail in the [Basics of Quantum Information](/learning/courses/basics-of-quantum-information) course.\n"
msgstr "Makna dan penggunaan get ini dijelaskan dengan lebih terperinci dalam kursus [Basics of Quantum Information](/learning/courses/basics-of-quantum-information).\n"

