#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-quantum-computing/bits-gates-and-circuits/extracted-outputs/e880f7eb-108c-4387-8ef4-97219fd5691c-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-quantum-computing/bits-gates-and-circuits/extracted-outputs/e880f7eb-108c-4387-8ef4-97219fd5691c-0.avif)\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Note: Qiskit bit ordering {#note-qiskit-bit-ordering}"
msgstr "Nota: Susunan bit Qiskit {#note-qiskit-bit-ordering}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Qiskit uses **Little Endian** notation when ordering qubits and bits, meaning **qubit 0 is the rightmost bit** in the bitstrings. Example: $|01\\rangle$ means q0 is $|1\\rangle$ and q1 is $|0\\rangle$. Be careful because some literature in quantum computing use the Big Endian notation (qubit 0 is the leftmost bit) and a great deal of quantum mechanics literature does, too.\n"
msgstr "Qiskit menggunakan notasi **Little Endian** untuk menyusun qubit dan bit, bermakna **qubit 0 ialah bit paling kanan** dalam rentetan bit. Contoh: $|01\\rangle$ bermaksud q0 ialah $|1\\rangle$ dan q1 ialah $|0\\rangle$. Berhati-hati kerana sebahagian literatur komputasi kuantum menggunakan notasi Big Endian (qubit 0 ialah bit paling kiri), dan banyak literatur mekanik kuantum juga berbuat demikian.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Another thing to notice is that when representing a quantum circuit, $|q_0\\rangle$ is always placed at the top of the circuit.\n"
"With this in mind, the quantum state of the above circuit can be written as a tensor product of single-qubit quantum state.\n"
msgstr ""
"Perkara lain yang perlu diperhatikan ialah apabila menggambarkan litar kuantum, $|q_0\\rangle$ sentiasa diletakkan di bahagian atas litar.\n"
"Dengan mengambil kira perkara ini, keadaan kuantum litar di atas boleh ditulis sebagai hasil darab tensor keadaan kuantum satu qubit.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$\n"
"|q1\\rangle \\otimes|q0\\rangle = (a|0\\rangle+b|1\\rangle) \\otimes (c|0\\rangle+d|1\\rangle)\n"
"$\n"
msgstr ""
"$\n"
"|q1\\rangle \\otimes|q0\\rangle = (a|0\\rangle+b|1\\rangle) \\otimes (c|0\\rangle+d|1\\rangle)\n"
"$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$\n"
"= ac|0\\rangle|0\\rangle+ad|0\\rangle|1\\rangle+bc|1\\rangle|0\\rangle+bd|1\\rangle|1\\rangle\n"
"$\n"
msgstr ""
"$\n"
"= ac|0\\rangle|0\\rangle+ad|0\\rangle|1\\rangle+bc|1\\rangle|0\\rangle+bd|1\\rangle|1\\rangle\n"
"$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$\n"
"= ac|00\\rangle+ad|01\\rangle+bc|10\\rangle+bd|11\\rangle\n"
"$\n"
msgstr ""
"$\n"
"= ac|00\\rangle+ad|01\\rangle+bc|10\\rangle+bd|11\\rangle\n"
"$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "( $|ac|^2+ |ad|^2+ |bc|^2+ |bd|^2=1$ )\n"
msgstr "( $|ac|^2+ |ad|^2+ |bc|^2+ |bd|^2=1$ )\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The initial state of Qiskit is $|0\\rangle|0\\rangle=|00\\rangle$, so by applying $H$ to each qubit, it changes to a state of equal superposition.\n"
msgstr "Keadaan awal Qiskit ialah $|0\\rangle|0\\rangle=|00\\rangle$, jadi dengan menerapkan $H$ pada setiap qubit, ia berubah kepada keadaan superposisi yang sama rata.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "$H|0\\rangle \\otimes H|0\\rangle=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(|0\\rangle+|1\\rangle) \\otimes \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(|0\\rangle+|1\\rangle) = \\frac{1}{2}(|00\\rangle+|01\\rangle+|10\\rangle+|11\\rangle)$\n"
msgstr "$H|0\\rangle \\otimes H|0\\rangle=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(|0\\rangle+|1\\rangle) \\otimes \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(|0\\rangle+|1\\rangle) = \\frac{1}{2}(|00\\rangle+|01\\rangle+|10\\rangle+|11\\rangle)$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"=\\frac{1}{2}\\left( \\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ 1 \\end{pmatrix} \\otimes \\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ 1 \\end{pmatrix}\\right) = \\frac{1}{2}\\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1 \\end{pmatrix}=\\frac{1}{2}\\left(\\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0 \\end{pmatrix}+\\begin{pmatrix} 0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0 \\end{pmatrix}+\\begin{pmatrix} 0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0 \\end{pmatrix}+\\begin{pmatrix} 0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1 \\end{pmatrix}\\right)\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"=\\frac{1}{2}\\left( \\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ 1 \\end{pmatrix} \\otimes \\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ 1 \\end{pmatrix}\\right) = \\frac{1}{2}\\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1 \\end{pmatrix}=\\frac{1}{2}\\left(\\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0 \\end{pmatrix}+\\begin{pmatrix} 0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0 \\end{pmatrix}+\\begin{pmatrix} 0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0 \\end{pmatrix}+\\begin{pmatrix} 0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1 \\end{pmatrix}\\right)\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The measurement rule is also same as a single qubit case, the probability of measuring $|00\\rangle$ is $|ac|^2$.\n"
msgstr "Peraturan pengukuran juga sama seperti kes satu qubit, kebarangkalian mengukur $|00\\rangle$ ialah $|ac|^2$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-quantum-computing/bits-gates-and-circuits/extracted-outputs/ebdf591f-18d0-4fd1-a3a3-b1cdac13bd97-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-quantum-computing/bits-gates-and-circuits/extracted-outputs/ebdf591f-18d0-4fd1-a3a3-b1cdac13bd97-0.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Next, let's measure this circuit.\n"
msgstr "Seterusnya, mari kita ukur litar ini.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-quantum-computing/bits-gates-and-circuits/extracted-outputs/2afdd5ac-e51a-4d94-9307-955cc8fbf821-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-quantum-computing/bits-gates-and-circuits/extracted-outputs/2afdd5ac-e51a-4d94-9307-955cc8fbf821-0.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Now, we will use a Aer simulator, again, to experimentally verify that the relative probabilities of all possible output states are roughly equal.\n"
msgstr "Sekarang, kita akan menggunakan simulator Aer sekali lagi untuk mengesahkan secara eksperimental bahawa kebarangkalian relatif semua keadaan output yang mungkin adalah lebih kurang sama.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-quantum-computing/bits-gates-and-circuits/extracted-outputs/060512ac-a106-4ecd-94f5-119048a08467-1.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-quantum-computing/bits-gates-and-circuits/extracted-outputs/060512ac-a106-4ecd-94f5-119048a08467-1.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "As expected, the states $|00\\rangle$, $|01\\rangle$, $|10\\rangle$, $|11\\rangle$ were measured almost 25% each.\n"
msgstr "Seperti yang dijangka, keadaan $|00\\rangle$, $|01\\rangle$, $|10\\rangle$, $|11\\rangle$ diukur hampir 25% setiap satu.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "4.2 Multi-qubit quantum gates {#42-multi-qubit-quantum-gates}"
msgstr "4.2 get kuantum pelbagai qubit {#42-multi-qubit-quantum-gates}"

#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "CNOT gate {#cnot-gate}"
msgstr "get CNOT {#cnot-gate}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A CNOT(\"controlled NOT\" or CX) gate is a two-qubit gate, meaning its action involves two qubits at once: the control qubit and the target qubit. A CNOT flips the target qubit only when the control qubit is $|1\\rangle$.\n"
msgstr "get CNOT (\"controlled NOT\" atau CX) ialah get dua qubit, bermakna tindakannya melibatkan dua qubit sekaligus: qubit kawalan dan qubit sasaran. CNOT membalikkan qubit sasaran hanya apabila qubit kawalan berada dalam keadaan $|1\\rangle$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Input (target,control) | Output (target,control) |\n"
"|:-----------:|:------------:|\n"
"| 00          | 00           |\n"
"| 01          | 11           |\n"
"| 10          | 10           |\n"
"| 11          | 01           |\n"
msgstr ""
"| Input (sasaran,kawalan) | Output (sasaran,kawalan) |\n"
"|:-----------:|:------------:|\n"
"| 00          | 00           |\n"
"| 01          | 11           |\n"
"| 10          | 10           |\n"
"| 11          | 01           |\n"

# doq: emptied 2026-09-05, previous translation failed check.py
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Let us first simulate the action of this two-qubit gate when q0 and q1 are both $|0\\rangle$, and obtain the output statevector. The Qiskit syntax used is ```qc.cx(control qubit, target qubit)```.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-quantum-computing/bits-gates-and-circuits/extracted-outputs/a5621efd-dd9f-4ea4-bf3a-be3cacb45287-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-quantum-computing/bits-gates-and-circuits/extracted-outputs/a5621efd-dd9f-4ea4-bf3a-be3cacb45287-0.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"As expected, applying a CNOT gate on $|00\\rangle$ did not change the state, since the control qubit was in the $|0\\rangle$ state.\n"
"Let's get back to our CNOT operation. This time we will apply a CNOT gate to $|01\\rangle$ and see what happens.\n"
msgstr ""
"Seperti yang dijangka, menerapkan get CNOT pada $|00\\rangle$ tidak mengubah keadaan, kerana qubit kawalan berada dalam keadaan $|0\\rangle$.\n"
"Mari kita kembali kepada operasi CNOT kita. Kali ini kita akan menerapkan get CNOT pada $|01\\rangle$ dan lihat apa yang berlaku.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-quantum-computing/bits-gates-and-circuits/extracted-outputs/5a02de82-44ff-40eb-b64c-2389d6eae3ee-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-quantum-computing/bits-gates-and-circuits/extracted-outputs/5a02de82-44ff-40eb-b64c-2389d6eae3ee-0.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "By applying a CNOT gate, the $|01\\rangle$ state has now become $|11\\rangle$.\n"
msgstr "Dengan menerapkan get CNOT, keadaan $|01\\rangle$ kini telah menjadi $|11\\rangle$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Let us verify these results by running the circuit on a simulator.\n"
msgstr "Mari kita sahkan keputusan ini dengan menjalankan litar pada simulator.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-quantum-computing/bits-gates-and-circuits/extracted-outputs/abcafb77-20bf-4bb7-bf8d-57f33af280c1-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-quantum-computing/bits-gates-and-circuits/extracted-outputs/abcafb77-20bf-4bb7-bf8d-57f33af280c1-0.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-quantum-computing/bits-gates-and-circuits/extracted-outputs/88b76f1d-083b-4f28-b415-380738d22599-1.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-quantum-computing/bits-gates-and-circuits/extracted-outputs/88b76f1d-083b-4f28-b415-380738d22599-1.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The results should show you that $|11\\rangle$ has been measured with 100% probability.\n"
msgstr "Keputusan seharusnya menunjukkan bahawa $|11\\rangle$ telah diukur dengan kebarangkalian 100%.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "4.3 Quantum entanglement and execution on a real quantum device {#43-quantum-entanglement-and-execution-on-a-real-quantum-device}"
msgstr "4.3 Keterjeratan kuantum dan pelaksanaan pada peranti kuantum sebenar {#43-quantum-entanglement-and-execution-on-a-real-quantum-device}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Let's start by introducing a specific entangled state which is particularly important in quantum computation, then we'll define the term \"entangled\":\n"
msgstr "Mari kita mulakan dengan memperkenalkan satu keadaan keterjeratan tertentu yang sangat penting dalam komputasi kuantum, kemudian kita akan takrifkan istilah \"keterjeratan\":\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}|00\\rangle + \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}|11\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
"and this state is called a **Bell state**.\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}|00\\rangle + \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}|11\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
"dan keadaan ini dipanggil **keadaan Bell**.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "An entangled state is a state $|\\psi_{AB}\\rangle$ consisting of quantum states $|\\psi_A\\rangle$ and $|\\psi_B\\rangle$ that cannot be represented by a tensor product of individual quantum states.\n"
msgstr "Keadaan keterjeratan ialah keadaan $|\\psi_{AB}\\rangle$ yang terdiri daripada keadaan kuantum $|\\psi_A\\rangle$ dan $|\\psi_B\\rangle$ yang tidak boleh diwakili oleh hasil darab tensor keadaan kuantum individu.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "If $|\\psi_{AB}\\rangle$ below has two states $|\\psi\\rangle_A$ and $|\\psi\\rangle_B$;\n"
msgstr "Jika $|\\psi_{AB}\\rangle$ di bawah mempunyai dua keadaan $|\\psi\\rangle_A$ dan $|\\psi\\rangle_B$;\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"|\\psi_{AB}\\rangle = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(|00\\rangle +|11\\rangle) = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(|0\\rangle_A|0\\rangle_B +|1\\rangle_A|1\\rangle_B)\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"|\\psi_{AB}\\rangle = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(|00\\rangle +|11\\rangle) = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(|0\\rangle_A|0\\rangle_B +|1\\rangle_A|1\\rangle_B)\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"|\\psi\\rangle_A = a_0|0\\rangle+a_1|1\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
"$$\n"
"|\\psi\\rangle_B = b_0|0\\rangle+b_1|1\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"|\\psi\\rangle_A = a_0|0\\rangle+a_1|1\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
"$$\n"
"|\\psi\\rangle_B = b_0|0\\rangle+b_1|1\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "the tensor product of these two states is the following\n"
msgstr "hasil darab tensor kedua-dua keadaan ini adalah seperti berikut\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"|\\psi\\rangle _A\\otimes |\\psi\\rangle _B = a_0 b_0|00\\rangle+a_0 b_1|01\\rangle+a_1 b_0|10\\rangle+a_1 b_1|11\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"|\\psi\\rangle _A\\otimes |\\psi\\rangle _B = a_0 b_0|00\\rangle+a_0 b_1|01\\rangle+a_1 b_0|10\\rangle+a_1 b_1|11\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "but there are no coefficients $a_0, a_1, b_0, $ and $b_1$ to satisfy these two equations. Therefore, $|\\psi_{AB}\\rangle$ is not represented by a tensor product of individual quantum state, $|\\psi\\rangle_A$ and $|\\psi\\rangle_B$, and this means that $|\\psi_{AB}\\rangle =  \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(|00\\rangle +|11\\rangle)$ is entangled state.\n"
msgstr "tetapi tiada pekali $a_0, a_1, b_0,$ dan $b_1$ yang boleh memenuhi kedua-dua persamaan ini. Oleh itu, $|\\psi_{AB}\\rangle$ tidak boleh diwakili oleh hasil darab tensor keadaan kuantum individu, $|\\psi\\rangle_A$ dan $|\\psi\\rangle_B$, dan ini bermakna $|\\psi_{AB}\\rangle =  \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(|00\\rangle +|11\\rangle)$ ialah keadaan yang terjerat.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Let us create the Bell state and run it on a real quantum computer. Now we will follow the four steps to writing a quantum program, called **Qiskit patterns**:\n"
msgstr "Mari kita cipta keadaan Bell dan jalankan pada komputer kuantum sebenar. Sekarang kita akan ikuti empat langkah untuk menulis program kuantum, yang dipanggil **corak Qiskit**:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '    1. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Map problem to quantum circuits and operators\n"
msgstr "Petakan masalah kepada litar dan pengendali kuantum\n"

#. type: Bullet: '    2. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Optimize for target hardware\n"
msgstr "Optimumkan untuk perkakasan sasaran\n"

#. type: Bullet: '    3. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Execute on target hardware\n"
msgstr "Laksanakan pada perkakasan sasaran\n"

#. type: Bullet: '    4. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Post-process the results\n"
msgstr "Proses selepas keputusan\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 1. Map problem to quantum circuits and operators {#step-1-map-problem-to-quantum-circuits-and-operators}"
msgstr "Langkah 1. Petakan masalah kepada litar dan pengendali kuantum {#step-1-map-problem-to-quantum-circuits-and-operators}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In a quantum program, quantum circuits are the native format in which to represent quantum instructions. When creating a circuit, you'll usually create a new QuantumCircuit object, then add instructions to it in sequence.\n"
msgstr "Dalam program kuantum, litar kuantum ialah format asli untuk mewakili arahan kuantum. Apabila mencipta litar, anda biasanya akan mencipta objek QuantumCircuit baru, kemudian menambah arahan ke dalamnya secara berurutan.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The following code cell creates a circuit that produces a Bell state, the specific two-qubit entangled state from above.\n"
msgstr "Sel kod berikut mencipta litar yang menghasilkan keadaan Bell, iaitu keadaan keterjeratan dua qubit khusus dari atas tadi.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-quantum-computing/bits-gates-and-circuits/extracted-outputs/5fdd9317-8fab-46ee-ac6d-25ef031dd52b-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-quantum-computing/bits-gates-and-circuits/extracted-outputs/5fdd9317-8fab-46ee-ac6d-25ef031dd52b-0.avif)\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 2. Optimize for target hardware {#step-2-optimize-for-target-hardware}"
msgstr "Langkah 2. Optimumkan untuk perkakasan sasaran {#step-2-optimize-for-target-hardware}"

#. type: Plain text
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
#| msgid ""
#| "Qiskit converts abstract circuits to QISA (Quantum Instruction Set Architecture) circuits that respect the constraints of the target hardware and optimizes circuit performance. So before the optimization, we will specify the target hardware.\n"
#| "If you do not have `qiskit-ibm-runtime`, you will need to install this first. For more information about Qiskit Runtime, [check out the API reference.](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/runtime-service)\n"
msgid ""
"Qiskit converts abstract circuits to QISA (Quantum Instruction Set Architecture) circuits that respect the constraints of the target hardware and optimizes circuit performance. So before the optimization, we will specify the target hardware.\n"
"If you do not have `qiskit-ibm-runtime`, you will need to install this first. For more information, [check out the API reference](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/runtime-service).\n"
msgstr ""
"Qiskit menukar litar abstrak kepada litar QISA (Quantum Instruction Set Architecture) yang mematuhi kekangan perkakasan sasaran dan mengoptimumkan prestasi litar. Jadi sebelum pengoptimuman, kita akan tentukan perkakasan sasaran.\n"
"Jika anda tidak mempunyai `qiskit-ibm-runtime`, anda perlu memasangnya terlebih dahulu. Untuk maklumat lanjut tentang Qiskit Runtime, [lihat rujukan API.](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/runtime-service)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We will specify the target hardware.\n"
msgstr "Kita akan tentukan perkakasan sasaran.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Transpiling the circuit is yet another complex process. Very briefly, this rewrites the circuit into a logically equivalent one using \"native gates\" (gates that a particular quantum computer can implement) and maps the qubits in your circuit to optimal real qubits on the target quantum computer. For more on transpilation, see this [documentation](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/transpiler#overview).\n"
msgstr "Transpilasi litar adalah satu lagi proses yang kompleks. Secara ringkas, ini menulis semula litar kepada litar yang setara secara logik menggunakan \"gate asli\" (gate yang boleh dilaksanakan oleh komputer kuantum tertentu) dan memetakan qubit dalam litar anda kepada qubit sebenar yang optimum pada komputer kuantum sasaran. Untuk maklumat lanjut tentang transpilasi, lihat [dokumentasi](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/transpiler#overview) ini.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "You can see that in the transpilation the circuit was rewritten using new gates. For more information, refer to the [ECRGate](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.library.ECRGate#ecrgate) documentation.\n"
msgstr "Anda boleh lihat bahawa dalam transpilasi, litar telah ditulis semula menggunakan gate baru. Untuk maklumat lanjut, rujuk dokumentasi [ECRGate](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.library.ECRGate#ecrgate).\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 3. Execute the target circuit {#step-3-execute-the-target-circuit}"
msgstr "Langkah 3. Laksanakan litar sasaran {#step-3-execute-the-target-circuit}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Now, we will run the target circuit on the real device.\n"
msgstr "Sekarang, kita akan menjalankan litar sasaran pada peranti sebenar.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Execution on the real device might require waiting in a queue, since quantum computers are valuable resources, and very much in demand. The job_id is used to check the execution status and results of the job later.\n"
msgstr "Pelaksanaan pada peranti sebenar mungkin memerlukan menunggu dalam giliran, kerana komputer kuantum adalah sumber yang berharga dan sangat diminati. job_id digunakan untuk menyemak status pelaksanaan dan keputusan kerja kemudian.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "You can also check the job status from your IBM Quantum dashboard：https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/workloads\n"
msgstr "Anda juga boleh menyemak status kerja dari papan pemuka IBM Quantum anda：https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/workloads\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 4. Post-process the results {#step-4-post-process-the-results}"
msgstr "Langkah 4. Proses selepas keputusan {#step-4-post-process-the-results}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Finally, we must post-process our results to create outputs in the expected format, like values or graphs.\n"
msgstr "Akhir sekali, kita mesti memproses keputusan kita untuk mencipta output dalam format yang dijangka, seperti nilai atau graf.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "As you can see, $|00\\rangle$ and $|11\\rangle$ are the most frequently observed. There are a few results other than the expected data, and they are due to noise and qubit decoherence. We will learn more about errors and noise in quantum computers in the later lessons of this course.\n"
msgstr "Seperti yang dapat dilihat, $|00\\rangle$ dan $|11\\rangle$ adalah yang paling kerap diperhatikan. Terdapat beberapa keputusan selain daripada data yang dijangka, dan ia disebabkan oleh hingar dan penyahrincian qubit. Kita akan belajar lebih lanjut tentang ralat dan hingar dalam komputer kuantum dalam pelajaran-pelajaran kemudian dalam kursus ini.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "4.4 GHZ state {#44-ghz-state}"
msgstr "4.4 Keadaan GHZ {#44-ghz-state}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The concept of entanglement can be extended to systems of more than two qubits. The GHZ state (Greenberger-Horne-Zeilinger state) is a maximally entangled state of three or more qubits. The GHZ state for three qubits is defined as\n"
msgstr "Konsep keterjeratan boleh diperluaskan kepada sistem lebih daripada dua qubit. Keadaan GHZ (keadaan Greenberger-Horne-Zeilinger) ialah keadaan yang terjerat sepenuhnya bagi tiga atau lebih qubit. Keadaan GHZ bagi tiga qubit ditakrifkan sebagai\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\frac{1}{\\sqrt 2}(|000\\rangle + |111\\rangle)\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\frac{1}{\\sqrt 2}(|000\\rangle + |111\\rangle)\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "It can be created with the following quantum circuit.\n"
msgstr "Ia boleh dicipta dengan litar kuantum berikut.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-quantum-computing/bits-gates-and-circuits/extracted-outputs/459b6162-3a54-41fe-9b67-9c1f8e731ebc-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-quantum-computing/bits-gates-and-circuits/extracted-outputs/459b6162-3a54-41fe-9b67-9c1f8e731ebc-0.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The \"depth\" of a quantum circuit is a useful and common metric to describe quantum circuits. Trace a path through the quantum circuit, moving left to right, only changing qubits when they are connected by a multi-qubit gate. Count the number of gates along that path. The maximum number of gates for any such path through a circuit is the depth. In modern noisy quantum computers, low-depth circuits have fewer errors and are likely to return good results. Very deep circuits are not.\n"
msgstr "\"Kedalaman\" litar kuantum ialah metrik yang berguna dan lazim untuk menggambarkan litar kuantum. Jejaki laluan melalui litar kuantum, bergerak dari kiri ke kanan, hanya menukar qubit apabila ia disambungkan oleh get pelbagai qubit. Kira bilangan get di sepanjang laluan tersebut. Bilangan maksimum get untuk mana-mana laluan sedemikian melalui litar ialah kedalamannya. Dalam komputer kuantum berderau moden, litar berkedalaman rendah mempunyai lebih sedikit ralat dan berkemungkinan besar memberikan keputusan yang baik. litar yang sangat dalam tidak begitu.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Using `QuantumCircuit.depth()`, we can check the depth of our quantum circuit. The depth of the above circuit is 4. The top qubit has only three gates including the measurement. But there is a path from the top qubit down to either qubit 1 or qubit 2 which involves another CNOT gate.\n"
msgstr "Menggunakan `QuantumCircuit.depth()`, kita boleh menyemak kedalaman litar kuantum kita. Kedalaman litar di atas ialah 4. qubit paling atas hanya mempunyai tiga get termasuk pengukuran. Tetapi terdapat laluan dari qubit paling atas ke sama ada qubit 1 atau qubit 2 yang melibatkan satu get CNOT lagi.\n"

